TEXT -80 -400 Left 5 ;Simple simulation of the skin effect (qualitative)\n=====================================\n( The skin resistance is altered via a given external frequency value )
TEXT 184 -232 Left 2 ;V(N003,N004)
TEXT -320 -320 Left 2 ;In this example you can see the large voltage drop\nat the inductive part of the netimpedance \nand their frequency behaviour \nThere are two frequencies present \nThe transient high frequency of about 1500Hz and the\nsteady state frequency of 50Hz. \nYou can see that under the 1500Hz signal the 50Hz signal is hidden\nShow also the voltage and hidden frequency of the netimpedance of the circuit below without skin resistance\nTo do this change line:\nE1 in 0 VALUE={V(N003,N004)} tripdv=1 tripdt=1 to\nE1 in 0 VALUE={V(N015,N016)} tripdv=1 tripdt=1\nYou can show also the hidden frequency at the current \nE1 in 0 VALUE={I(V1)} tripdv=1 tripdt=1
TEXT 144 -104 Left 2 ;This is the 50Hz reference
TEXT 208 80 Left 2 !.subckt 1470Hz_2 in out params: tenable=1u ; Bandstop 1450 - 1550 \n* Butterworth filter order 2 \nE1 in1 0 VALUE={IF(time>tenable,v(in),0)} tripdv=1 tripdt=1\nL1 in1 out 10.72m\nC1 in1 out 1.125u\nL2 out L1rms2 2.251H\nC2 L1rms2 0 5.359nF\nR1 out 0 1000ohm\n.ends
TEXT 208 40 Left 2 !E1 in 0 VALUE={V(N003,N004)} tripdv=1 tripdt=1\nx1470_4 in out1 1470Hz_4 params: tenable=1u\nx1470_2 in out2 1470Hz_2 params: tenable=1u
TEXT -256 16 Left 2 !.subckt 1470Hz_4 in out params: tenable=1u ; 1200-1800Hz Bandstop\n* Butterworth filter order 4\n* https://rf-tools.com/lc-filter/\nE1 in1 0 VALUE={IF(time>tenable,v(in),0)} tripdv=1 tripdt=1\nL1 in1 out1 67.67m\nC1 in1 out1 173.3n\nL2 out1 L1rms1 168.2m\nC2 L1rms1 0 69.73n\nL11 out1 out 47.85m\nC11 out1 out 245.1n\nL21 out L1rms2 693.2m\nC21 L1rms2 0 16.92n\nR1 out 0 1000ohm\n.ends
